# Tria Smart Contract Security Audit Case Study

## Overview
QuillAudits conducted a comprehensive security audit for Tria, a self-custodial crypto neobank and interoperability platform designed to simplify digital asset management across multiple blockchains.

The engagement focused on strengthening authentication flows, wallet ownership validation, claim security, smart contract logic, and infrastructure hardening.

## Scope
- Smart Contract Security Review
- Authentication & Authorization Testing
- Wallet Signature Validation
- Frontend & Backend Security Assessment
- Infrastructure & API Testing
- Threat Modelling & Vulnerability Analysis

## Technologies Involved
- Solidity
- Ethereum
- ERC20
- Web3 Authentication
- DeFi Infrastructure
- Smart Contracts

## Key Findings
- Missing authentication on critical claim endpoints
- Wallet signature verification gaps
- Potential gas-griefing vectors
- Emergency withdrawal logic concerns
- Ownership transfer security improvements
- Frontend security hardening opportunities

## Security Improvements
- Implemented stronger authentication validation
- Added signature-based ownership verification
- Secured sensitive infrastructure components
- Improved contract safety mechanisms
- Strengthened access control and claim security

## Audit Outcome
All identified findings were reviewed with the Tria team and remediation guidance was provided to improve platform security, reliability, and user fund protection.

